{"aggregate_id": "01M38VVH6ZG5DX5ASSPBX61002", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M38VVH7PYSWZ65GXR6AWB6CF", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn@sddevelopment.be", "created_at": "2026-09-24T04:47:49.997908+00:00", "friendly_name": "Coord Reads Fail Closed", "mission_id": "01M38VVH6ZG5DX5ASSPBX61002", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "coord-read-fail-closed-01M38VVH", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "On a coord-topology mission from a checkout where the coordination worktree is not materialised (a fresh clone, a CI runner, a removed worktree), two commands read through an empty or status-only coordination surface and then act on it as if it were the real document: tracer-append rewrites a traces file from an empty default (destroying every earlier finding, exit 0), and the decision ledger resolves to a status-only husk that blocks a mission's acceptance with no CLI way out. This mission makes those reads fail closed against the authoritative file instead of clobbering or split-braining it. Closes #4959 and #4966 (siblings under epic #5002).", "purpose_tldr": "Stop an unmaterialised coordination surface from silently overwriting or hiding a teammate's real mission files during ordinary coord-topology commands.", "target_branch": "fix/coord-read-fail-closed", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T04:47:50.006604+00:00"}
